    "headRefOid": "6f16090081012e3a8aea4e1d5a4ac08fe2f3bd1f",
    "title": "feat(serve): add POST /v1/internal/reload for parser and template hot-reload",
    "url": "https://github.com/1CatAI/1Cat-vLLM/pull/1439",
    "body": "## Motivation\n\nIterating on a tool parser or a chat template means restarting the engine, which costs minutes of model load. For deployments serving from a mutable source tree that is the dominant cost of the edit → test loop.\n\n## Change\n\n`POST /v1/internal/reload` applies both changes in a single request.\n\n### Tool parsers (`tool_parsers/_hotreload.py`)\n\nReloads every already-imported `vllm.tool_parsers.*` module — prerequisites (`utils`, `qwen_xml_tool_grammar`) first, then the parsers — and points the lazy registry at the new class objects. A module that fails to reload keeps its old version rather than taking the server down over a typo in the file being edited.\n\nModules are discovered from `sys.modules` rather than a hardcoded list, so new parsers are covered without touching this file.\n\n### Serving classes\n\nLive serving objects (`app.state`) are long-lived and stay bound to the classes they were constructed from — `importlib.reload` creates *new* classes that nothing holds. Rebuilding the objects is not an option (they own the tokenizer, engine client and renderer), so the new class's own attributes are copied onto the old class. Method lookup goes through the class, so the change takes effect immediately and instance state is untouched. Only the class's own attributes are copied, never inherited base behaviour.\n\n### Chat template (`chat_utils.py`)\n\n`load_chat_template` records a file-backed source; the endpoint re-reads it and pushes it onto the holders. This is deliberately **not** an mtime stat per request — the request path pays nothing, and re-reading happens only when the endpoint is called.\n\n## Safety\n\nRegistered unconditionally but inert when nothing was edited. Intended for development and verification.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Edit a parser body → curl the endpoint → the next request uses the new code, no restart.\n- Edit a chat template file → curl → subsequent requests render with the new template.\n- Introduce a syntax error in a parser → the endpoint reports the failure and the old parser keeps serving.",
